Below is a short “data‑discovery road‑map” for the task, followed by ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (simple → complex).  
Every referenced identifier is wrapped in double quotes and qualified with DATABASE.SCHEMA.TABLE as requested.

───────────────────────────────────────────  
Relevant columns and their potential use  
───────────────────────────────────────────  

NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.GSOD2015  
• "wban": filter on Central Park weather station ('94728').  
• "year", "mo", "da": filter for 2015‑07‑15.  
• "temp": average temperature to decide the “highest average temperature” criteria.

NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.STATIONS  
• "wban", "name", "lat", "lon": confirm the location / meta data of WBAN 94728.

NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS  
• "starttime", "stoptime": time stamp of each trip (µs).  
• "start_station_latitude", "start_station_longitude": point for spatial match to a ZIP polygon.  
• "end_station_latitude", "end_station_longitude": point for spatial match to a ZIP polygon.  
• "start_station_id", "end_station_id": additional key if the stations look‑up table is preferred.  

NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_STATIONS  
• "station_id", "latitude", "longitude": canonical geometry of each station – can be joined to trips via IDs when needed.

NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES  
• "zip_code": the 5‑digit ZIP.  
• "zip_code_geom": polygon – use ST_WITHIN to see whether a point lies inside.  
• "state_code": keep only NY (or neighbouring) if necessary.

Typical filters / join predicates that will be useful  
•  GSOD2015:  WHERE "wban" = '94728' AND "year" = '2015' AND "mo" = '07' AND "da" = '15'  
•  Trips on 15‑Jul‑2015:  
   WHERE TO_DATE( TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("starttime" / 1000000) ) = '2015‑07‑15'  
•  Spatial start‑zip match:  
   ST_WITHIN( TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || "start_station_longitude" || ' ' || "start_station_latitude" || ')'),  
              TO_GEOGRAPHY(z."zip_code_geom") )  
•  Same pattern for end‑zip.  
•  Ranking rule: ORDER BY start‑zip ASC, end‑zip DESC  (smallest start‑zip, largest end‑zip).  

───────────────────────────────────────────  
Ten incremental Snowflake queries (LIMIT 20)  
───────────────────────────────────────────  

```sql
--1️⃣  Description: Verify Central Park station (WBAN 94728) in the meta table.
SELECT
  "wban",
  "name",
  "lat",
  "lon",
  "begin",
  "end"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.STATIONS
WHERE "wban" = '94728'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2️⃣  Description: Pull the Central Park weather record for 15‑Jul‑2015.
SELECT
  "wban",
  "year",
  "mo",
  "da",
  "temp"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.GSOD2015
WHERE "wban" = '94728'
  AND "year" = '2015'
  AND "mo" = '07'
  AND "da" = '15'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3️⃣  Description: Compare all WBANs’ average temperature for that date (sanity check).
SELECT
  "wban",
  "temp"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.GSOD2015
WHERE "year" = '2015'
  AND "mo" = '07'
  AND "da" = '15'
ORDER BY "temp" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4️⃣  Description: Sample Citi Bike trips that started on 15‑Jul‑2015 (raw rows).
SELECT
  "starttime",
  "stoptime",
  "start_station_id",
  "end_station_id",
  "start_station_latitude",
  "start_station_longitude",
  "end_station_latitude",
  "end_station_longitude"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS
WHERE TO_DATE( TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("starttime" / 1000000) ) = '2015‑07‑15'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5️⃣  Description: Distinct station coordinates used on 15‑Jul‑2015.
SELECT DISTINCT
  "start_station_id",
  "start_station_latitude",
  "start_station_longitude"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS
WHERE TO_DATE( TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("starttime" / 1000000) ) = '2015‑07‑15'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--6️⃣  Description: Peek at a few ZIP polygons located in New York State.
SELECT
  "zip_code",
  "state_code",
  "area_land_meters"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES
WHERE "state_code" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--7️⃣  Description: Attach a start‑ZIP to a handful of trips (spatial join).
SELECT
  t."start_station_id",
  TO_VARCHAR(z."zip_code") AS "start_zip"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS  t
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES       z
  ON ST_WITHIN(
       TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || t."start_station_longitude" || ' ' || t."start_station_latitude" || ')'),
       TO_GEOGRAPHY(z."zip_code_geom")
     )
WHERE TO_DATE( TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(t."starttime" / 1000000) ) = '2015‑07‑15'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--8️⃣  Description: Attach both start‑ and end‑ZIPs for trips on 15‑Jul‑2015 (small sample).
SELECT
  t."start_station_id",
  t."end_station_id",
  TO_VARCHAR(zs."zip_code") AS "start_zip",
  TO_VARCHAR(ze."zip_code") AS "end_zip"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS t
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES      zs
  ON ST_WITHIN(
       TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || t."start_station_longitude" || ' ' || t."start_station_latitude" || ')'),
       TO_GEOGRAPHY(zs."zip_code_geom")
     )
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES      ze
  ON ST_WITHIN(
       TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || t."end_station_longitude" || ' ' || t."end_station_latitude" || ')'),
       TO_GEOGRAPHY(ze."zip_code_geom")
     )
WHERE TO_DATE( TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(t."starttime" / 1000000) ) = '2015‑07‑15'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--9️⃣  Description: Determine the min start‑ZIP and max end‑ZIP per trip on that date.
SELECT
  TO_VARCHAR(zs."zip_code") AS "start_zip",
  TO_VARCHAR(ze."zip_code") AS "end_zip"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS t
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES      zs
  ON ST_WITHIN(
       TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || t."start_station_longitude" || ' ' || t."start_station_latitude" || ')'),
       TO_GEOGRAPHY(zs."zip_code_geom")
     )
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES      ze
  ON ST_WITHIN(
       TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || t."end_station_longitude" || ' ' || t."end_station_latitude" || ')'),
       TO_GEOGRAPHY(ze."zip_code_geom")
     )
WHERE TO_DATE( TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(t."starttime" / 1000000) ) = '2015‑07‑15'
ORDER BY "start_zip" ASC, "end_zip" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--🔟  Description: Final selection – candidate trip that (a) occurs on 2015-07-15,
--                 (b) has both start & end ZIPs inside NY polygons, ordered by
--                 smallest start‑ZIP then largest end‑ZIP (pick first row).
SELECT
  TO_VARCHAR(zs."zip_code") AS "starting_zip",
  TO_VARCHAR(ze."zip_code") AS "ending_zip"
FROM NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS t
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES      zs
  ON ST_WITHIN(
       TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || t."start_station_longitude" || ' ' || t."start_station_latitude" || ')'),
       TO_GEOGRAPHY(zs."zip_code_geom")
     )
JOIN NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES      ze
  ON ST_WITHIN(
       TO_GEOGRAPHY('POINT(' || t."end_station_longitude" || ' ' || t."end_station_latitude" || ')'),
       TO_GEOGRAPHY(ze."zip_code_geom")
     )
WHERE TO_DATE( TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(t."starttime" / 1000000) ) = '2015‑07‑15'
  AND zs."state_code" = 'NY'
  AND ze."state_code" = 'NY'
ORDER BY "starting_zip" ASC, "ending_zip" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progressively surface all pieces needed to derive “the trip whose start and end ZIP Code areas have the highest average temperature on 15‑Jul‑2015 as measured by WBAN 94728”, ending with the candidate list ordered by the required ZIP prioritisation rule.
